● Summary of Findings

  Based on my analysis of the VIctory GPU memory system, here are the key findings for reducing frame time and VRAM
  consumption:

  Most Impactful Finding: SPECULATIVE_COPIES Constant

  Location: crates/victory-gpu/src/memory.rs:70
  const SPECULATIVE_COPIES: usize = crate::descriptor::host::FIRST_RAW_PAGE_SLOTS as usize - 1;
  Current value: 1023 (since FIRST_RAW_PAGE_SLOTS = 1024)

  This is the primary VRAM control knob - it directly limits the maximum number of copy pages, which directly controls
  VRAM consumption.

  How It Works

  - When map_page() is called and copies.len() >= SPECULATIVE_COPIES, speculative mapping is skipped
  - The speculative_skips counter is incremented
  - Pages remain available for later allocation via roots, constants, or faults
  - In populate(), the same limit applies mid-buffer with partial_copy tracking for later completion

  Test-Verified Behavior

  From producer_tests.rs:635: When 1029 pages are requested, copies cap at 1023 and speculative_skips > 0 is asserted.

