  Diagnostic Metrics to Monitor

  From ready() tracing output (lines 558-562):
  - copies - Total numbered copies (direct VRAM indicator)
  - deferred_speculation (speculative_skips) - How often limit was hit
  - shader_faults (from_faults) - Copies from page faults
  - ownership_changes - Other copy sources

  Recommended Approach

  1. Make SPECULATIVE_COPIES configurable via victory.toml or environment variable (default 1023)
  2. Profile baseline with current value to record speculative_skips, from_faults, and copies count
  3. Test reduced values (512 → 256) and measure impact on VRAM, frame time, and correctness
  4. Consider adaptive logic based on detected hardware (lower on integrated GPUs)

  Other Notable Findings

  - Page refusal handling (lines 378-389): Pages consistently refused are tracked and cleared each frame
  - Fault-based allocation (lines 432-462): Pages without copies are allocated on next frame via take_faults()
  - Partial copy support (lines 409-421): Allows confirmed accesses to expand coverage after speculative limit hit
  - Reconciliation loop (lines 287-329): Per-frame optimization that clears refused set and checks generation changes

  All analysis was performed without requiring project installation - derived entirely from code review of the existing
